# prompt: cartoon boing, springy bounce
# tags: boing, spring, bounce, cartoon
# A short delay at high feedback is not an echo here, it is the spring: the
# recirculation *is* the coil, the same way `helicopter` builds a rotor out of
# one thump. The header has to pay for it — the delay keeps sounding for half a
# second after the envelope closed, because the chain runs after the envelope.
sound "boing" 800ms
  spring: chirp tri ~900Hz[400..1800] -> 180Hz in 200ms >> delay ~45ms[20..80] feedback 0.55 mix 0.5 | gain 0.4 decay 260ms
  body: tone sine ~200Hz[100..420] -> 120Hz in 160ms | gain 0.2 decay 220ms
